## Summary
Vince Buyssens reviews reference websites to guide the design of his agency's site and client proposals. He highlights preferred layouts, typography, and diagram styles, emphasizing clean, centered structures, straight corners, and isometric SVG visualizations.

## Segments
[00:00.0-02:25.0] Vince reviews Hex/Tensorlake, highlighting alignment, diagrams, and spacing.
[02:25.0-05:00.0] Vince analyzes Unsiloed, praising its centered layout, straight corners, and sticky scroll isometric diagrams.
[05:00.0-05:51.0] Vince looks at Rollups, noting its centered structure and breathing room.
[05:51.0-06:31.0] Vince reviews Lighthouse, appreciating the layout but disliking rounded corners.
[06:31.0-07:07.0] Vince examines Atomic Tessellator, focusing on isometric visuals and particle systems.
[07:07.0-07:42.0] Vince looks at Cluster, specifically admiring a workflow diagram.
[07:42.0-08:00.0] Vince briefly shows Enerblock, noting its info clustering.
[08:00.0-08:39.0] Vince reviews Augustus, liking its stacked layout and blue diagrams.
[08:39.0-08:59.0] Vince checks Prime Intellect, finding it dense but with good diagrams.
[08:59.0-09:14.0] Vince looks at Euclid, pointing out centered elements.
[09:14.0-09:51.0] Vince examines Spade, liking the visuals but not the background video diagrams.
[09:51.0-10:18.0] Vince views Cofounder, appreciating the typography.
[10:18.0-10:41.0] Vince reviews CCTP, liking its technical feel.
[10:41.0-10:48.0] Vince briefly scrolls through Vite.
[10:48.0-11:09.0] Vince looks at NoGood Studio, noting its centered creative layout.
[11:09.0-11:21.0] Vince shows Dispatch, praising its technical aesthetic and fonts.
[11:21.0-11:43.0] Vince briefly recaps previous sites.
[11:43.0-12:28.2] Vince reviews Arrakis, highlighting its centered layout and visualizations.

